Here is the goal model based on the mission description:

### Goal Model

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|--------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1     | Deliver All Resources | Ensure all required resources are delivered to the specified location. | - | Achieve | - |
| G2     | Collect All Resources | Gather all required resources from their respective storage locations. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G3     | Deliver All Collected Resources | Transport all collected resources to the specified delivery location. | ; | Perform | G1 |
| G2.1   | Collect Resource R1 | Retrieve resource R1 from its storage location. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G2.2   | Collect Resource R2 | Retrieve resource R2 from its storage location. | - | Perform | G2 |
| G3.1   | Deliver Resource R1 | Transport resource R1 to the delivery location. | - | Perform | G3 |
| G3.2   | Deliver Resource R2 | Transport resource R2 to the delivery location. | - | Perform | G3 |

### Task Model

| Task ID | Task Title | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|------------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|----------------|
| AT2.1.1 | Collect R1 | Retrieve resource R1 from storage. | AND | Storage A | 1 | Single robot assigned to collect R1. |
| AT2.1.2 | Fallback Collect R1 | Another robot collects R1 if primary fails. | FALLBACK(AT2.1.1) | Storage A | 1 | Fallback for low battery or failure. |
| AT3.1.1 | Deliver R1 | Transport R1 to delivery location. | AND | Delivery Point | 1 | Single robot assigned to deliver R1. |
| AT3.1.2 | Fallback Deliver R1 | Another robot delivers R1 if primary fails. | FALLBACK(AT3.1.1) | Delivery Point | 1 | Fallback for low battery or failure. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both collection and delivery are necessary and must occur in sequence to achieve the mission.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [AND]**  
  Justification: All resources must be collected, so each resource's collection is an AND decomposition.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [AND]**  
  Justification: All resources must be delivered, so each resource's delivery is an AND decomposition.

- **G2.1 -> AT2.1.1, AT2.1.2 [FALLBACK(AT2.1.1)]**  
  Justification: If the primary robot fails (e.g., low battery), another robot takes over.

- **G3.1 -> AT3.1.1, AT3.1.2 [FALLBACK(AT3.1.1)]**  
  Justification: If the primary robot fails during delivery, another robot takes over.

This model ensures that all resources are collected and delivered efficiently, with fallback mechanisms in place for battery issues or failures.
